if something is both big and rough, it is not nice.\n12. **If something is big then it is nice**: This tells us that if something is big, it is nice.\n13. **If Bob is furry then Bob is young**: This tells us that if Bob is furry, he is young.\n14. **If something is furry then it is big**: This tells us that if something is furry, it is big.\n15. **If something is nice then it is kind**: This tells us that if something is nice, it is kind.\n\nNow, let\'s evaluate the statement "Bob is not green":.\n\n- From point 1, we know that Bob is green.\n- There is no information provided that contradicts or changes this fact.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "Bob is not green" is false.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
