big, it is young.\n10. **All red things are green.** This tells us that if something is red, it is green.\n11. **If something is kind then it is not red.** This tells us that if something is kind, it is not red.\n12. **All furry things are kind.** This tells us that if something is furry, it is kind.\n13. **If Harry is young then Harry is cold.** This tells us that if Harry is young, it is cold.\n14. **If something is young and cold then it is furry.** This tells us that if something is young and cold, it is furry.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Harry is red":.\n\n- We know that Harry is green (from point 6).\n- We also know that all red things are green (from point 10).\n- Therefore, if Harry were red, it would have to be green, which contradicts the fact that Harry is green.\n\nBased on this analysis, the statement "Harry is red" is false because it contradicts the information provided about Harry\'s color.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
