things are blue.** This tells us that Fiona is blue because she is round.\n\nNow, let\'s combine these pieces of information to determine if Gary is big:.\n\n- We know that Gary is smart (from point 7).\n- We know that Gary is furry (from point 8).\n- We know that Gary is blue (from point 12).\n- We know that big, blue things are round (from point 9).\n\nSince Gary is blue and big, and we know that big, blue things are round, it follows that Gary is round. However, we also know that round things are cold (from point 13), and we know that Gary is cold (from point 7). Therefore, Gary must be round and cold.\n\nGiven that Gary is round and cold, and we know that round things are blue (from point 15), it follows that Gary is blue. Since Gary is blue and big, and we know that big, blue things are round (from point 9), it follows that Gary is big.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Gary is big" is true based on the given information.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
