*.\n   - This tells us that if something is both blue and young, it will be red.\n\nNow, let\'s apply these rules to Gary:.\n\n- From rule 6, we know that if Gary is furry, then Gary is blue.\n- From rule 7, we know that if Gary is nice and big, then Gary is young.\n- From rule 9, we know that if Gary is blue and young, then Gary is red.\n\nSince Gary is furry (rule 6), we can conclude that Gary is blue (rule 6). Since Gary is nice (rule 8) and big (rule 7), we can conclude that Gary is young (rule 7). Therefore, Gary is blue and young (rules 6 and 9), which means Gary is red (rule 9).\n\nThus, the statement "Gary is red" is true based on the given information.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
