 is round.\n14. **All green things are big.** This tells us that if something is green, it is also big.\n15. **If Harry is young then Harry is furry.** This tells us that if Harry is in a youthful stage, he has fur.\n16. **Furry, smart things are nice.** This tells us that if something is both furry and smart, it is nice.\n\nNow, let\'s evaluate the statement "Harry is not green":.\n\n- From point 6, we know that Harry is smart.\n- From point 11, we know that if something is green, it is also big.\n- From point 12, we know that if something is green, it is also smart.\n- From point 13, we know that if something is green, it is also nice.\n- From point 15, we know that if Harry is young, he has fur.\n- From point 16, we know that if something is furry and smart, it is nice.\n\nSince Harry is smart (point 6) and all green things are smart (point 12), Harry must be green. Therefore, the statement "Harry is not green" is false.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
